							<article class=3D"message-body js-selectToQuote">
								<div class=3D"bbWrapper">Hello Eric,<br>
<br>
For whatever reason,<br>
OneNote files imported into RightNote using the following procedure,<br>
cannot be edited,<br>
even though the Toggle Edit Mode option is available in RightNote.<br>
<br>
A OneNote page with just text is slow to import.<br>
A OneNote page with lots of graphics will be even slower to import, <br>
so patience is required.<br>
<br>
Saving regular web pages to RightNote,<br>
such as JPSoft Forum pages,<br>
are fast,<br>
and can be easily edited once in RightNote.<br>
<br>
Personally,<br>
I just copy and paste from OneNote into RightNote when I need a specific no=
te.<br>
<br>
Still, here is the procedure for your review. <br>
Open the help file from RightNote.<br>
<br>
Do a search for SingleFile.<br>
<br>
(I think that Note #2 can be ignored in the help for SingleFile,<br>
since Rael fixed that for me back on August 19, 2024.<br>
as RightNote now uses the Edge/Chromium engine).<br>
<br>
Once you have SingleFile installed into your web browser,<br>
open your OneNote file in your web browser.<br>
<br>
My OneNote Notebook file is at <a href=3D"https://onedrive.live.com/" targe=
t=3D"_blank" class=3D"link link--external" rel=3D"nofollow ugc noopener">ht=
tps://onedrive.live.com</a> in my OneDrive.<br>
<br>
With the OneNote page open in your web browser,<br>
click Hide Navigation to hide the navigation bar on the left side of your s=
creen.<br>
That ensures your note is occupying all of the screen.<br>
<br>
Make sure that you have one,<br>
and only one,<br>
RightNote file open at this time. <br>
<br>
Click the SingleFile button in your web browsers toolbar.<br>
<br>
SingleFile will download the web page,<br>
then RightNote will intercept,<br>
and prompt you for the location to save the web page in your open RightNote=
 file.<br>
<br>
Things I have learned...<br>
<ul>
<li data-xf-list-type=3D"ul">Open the RightNote file to which you want to s=
ave the web page before saving a web page.</li>
<li data-xf-list-type=3D"ul">You can only have one RightNote file open on y=
our system,</li>
</ul>two or more open RightNote files confuses the SingleFile process.<br>
- A OneNote page with lots of graphics will be slow, so patience is require=
d.<br>
<br>
Here's how I have the options set for SingleFile in RightNote;<br>

=09

